/* V56 — four seconds out of five with nothing to tap.

   Measured, playing solo at six taps a second and dismissing the augment screen properly:

       with a player      median 0 hostiles on screen, p90 1, max 2, screen empty 79% of the time
       with no input      median 6 hostiles on screen, p90 13, max 14, screen empty 3%

   The spawner is not broken — left alone the arena fills up and overruns the reactor in eleven
   seconds. The problem is what happens once someone is actually playing: a competent player clears
   each hostile as it arrives and then waits for the next one. Forty-two kills in forty-five seconds,
   with four seconds in five spent looking at an empty screen.

   For a game whose entire verb is "tap the thing", that is the whole of the fun problem. Every other
   improvement — the art, the weapons, the sound — decorates a screen that is usually empty.

   Two things are deliberately *not* the fix.

   Not a faster base spawn rate: that would make the unattended arena lethal even sooner, and the
   no-input measurement above shows it is already lethal in eleven seconds. The game is not too easy
   when you ignore it; it is too empty when you engage with it.

   Not a hush change either. The hush was the first suspect — the trace showed it frozen at 1.5 for
   the whole run — but that turned out to be the measurement: the augment screen pauses the game, the
   harness was not dismissing it, and `v35Live()` is false while paused so nothing decremented. With
   the harness fixed the hush decays exactly as designed, about one second per wave advance, and
   accounts for 10% of the run. It is not the problem and is left alone.

   The fix is a floor on how empty the arena is allowed to get while somebody is playing it. It only
   ever pulls the next spawn *forward*, and only while the screen is below the floor, so it cannot
   slow the game down and cannot make a full screen fuller. A player who is keeping up gets more to
   do; a player who is drowning is already above the floor and is not touched at all. */

const V56={
 /* How many hostiles the arena tries to keep in front of the player. Grows with the wave so the
    early game still opens gently — two on screen at wave one is a tutorial, seven by wave ten is a
    fight — and caps so this never becomes its own difficulty curve on top of the real one. */
 floor:(wave)=>Math.min(7,2+Math.floor((wave-1)*.55)),
 /* How hard a deficit pulls the spawn timer down, in seconds of timer per second of real time per
    missing hostile. At 1.6 a screen three short of the floor recovers in well under a second, which
    is fast enough that the player never notices a gap and slow enough that hostiles arrive as a
    stream rather than a clump. */
 urgency:1.6,
 /* A hostile that has not entered the play area yet does not count as something to tap. This is the
    same y>0 test the bot's targeting uses, so the floor is measured against what a player can
    actually reach rather than against what exists. */
 minY:0
};

function v56Live(){
 return game.running
  &&!game.paused
  /* Duels replay one server-authoritative spawn list so both players meet identical enemies at
     identical moments. Same line V21 and V35 drew, for the same reason. */
  &&game.mode!=='duel'
  /* The hush is deliberate emptiness and is the one moment this must not fight. */
  &&!(game.v35Hush>0)
  /* A titan owns the screen and its own pacing; feeding a crowd in underneath it is a different
     fight from the one that was designed. */
  &&!game.boss;
}

const v56Update=update;
update=function(dt){
 v56Update(dt);
 if(!v56Live())return;
 let onScreen=0;
 for(const o of game.orbs)if(o.y>V56.minY)onScreen++;
 const deficit=V56.floor(game.wave)-onScreen;
 if(deficit<=0)return;
 /* Only ever brought forward, never pushed back: this is a floor on activity, not a replacement for
    the spawn schedule. `MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` is the base loop's way of saying "no more spawns this
    wave", and that has to be respected or a completed directive would keep producing hostiles. */
 if(game.spawnTimer===Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER)return;
 game.spawnTimer=Math.max(0,game.spawnTimer-dt*deficit*V56.urgency);
};
